config BR2_PACKAGE_AIC8800
	bool "aic8800"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	help
	  Out-of-tree AICSemi AIC8800-family Wi-Fi 6 (802.11ax) + Bluetooth
	  USB driver, plus the firmware blobs it cannot run without.
	  Two kernel modules (aic_load_fw, aic8800_fdrv) and ~6.6 MiB of
	  firmware under /lib/firmware/aic8800*/.

	  Covers the commodity cheap-AX dongle market that has no driver at
	  all in this image today: Tenda U2 (2604:0014), U11 (2604:001f),
	  U11 Pro (2604:0020), TX1U Nano (3625:0110), the TP-Link/Mercury
	  pair (2357:014b, 2357:014e) and 41 AICSemi-branded IDs under
	  a69c: and 368b:.

	  Mainline has NO aic8800 driver over any bus, in any tree checked
	  (6.18, 7.2, 7.3-rc) -- no chip HAL, no staging entry, no
	  MAINTAINERS line -- which is the one condition under which
	  ADR 0016 permits an out-of-tree fork. There are zero USB-ID bind
	  conflicts against the in-kernel drivers this image builds.

	  Sourced from radxa-pkg/aic8800, which packages the SAME AICSemi
	  SDK snapshot that MiSTer stock vendored into its 6.18 kernel fork
	  (RELEASE_DATE "2026_0123_5f7be68d"), and unlike stock also ships
	  the firmware. See package/aic8800/aic8800.mk for the provenance
	  chain, the vendor-patch policy, and the licence position; see
	  docs/wifi-parity.md section 10 for the decision record.

	  https://github.com/radxa-pkg/aic8800

comment "aic8800 needs a Linux kernel to be built"
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
